# stdlib.semver Tutorial

`stdlib.semver` implements Semantic Versioning 2.0.0 parsing, comparison, bumping, and range matching (`^` and `~`) without external dependencies.

## Core API

- `parse(version: str) -> list`: Parses `"v1.2.3-beta.1+build.42"` into `[1, 2, 3, "beta.1", "build.42"]`
- `format(major, minor, patch) -> str` / `format_full(major, minor, patch, pre, build) -> str` / `to_string(v) -> str`
- `major(v)`, `minor(v)`, `patch(v)`, `prerelease(v)`, `build_meta(v)`, `is_stable(v)`, `is_prerelease(v)`
- `compare(a, b) -> int`: Returns `-1`, `0`, or `1` (pre-release < stable; build metadata ignored)
- `eq(a, b)`, `lt(a, b)`, `gt(a, b)`, `lte(a, b)`, `gte(a, b)`
- `bump_major(v)`, `bump_minor(v)`, `bump_patch(v)`, `with_prerelease(v, pre)`, `with_build(v, build)`
- `satisfies_caret(v, major, minor)` (`^major.minor`) and `satisfies_tilde(v, major, minor)` (`~major.minor`)

## Runnable Example

See `examples/semver_tutorial.ltl` and `tests/stdlib_semver_tutorial.ltl`:

```lateralus
import semver

let v1 = parse("v1.2.3-beta.1+build.42")
let v2 = parse("1.2.3")
let v3 = parse("1.3.0")

assert(to_string(v1) == "1.2.3-beta.1+build.42")
assert(compare(v1, v2) == -1)
assert(eq(parse("1.2.3+a"), parse("1.2.3+b")))
assert(to_string(bump_minor(v2)) == "1.3.0")
assert(to_string(bump_major(v2)) == "2.0.0")
assert(satisfies_caret(v3, 1, 2) == true)
assert(satisfies_tilde(v3, 1, 2) == false)
```

## Pinned Test Vectors

| Input / Operation | Expected Output |
|---|---|
| `parse("v1.2.3-beta.1+build.42")` | `[1, 2, 3, "beta.1", "build.42"]` |
| `compare(parse("v1.2.3-beta.1+build.42"), parse("1.2.3"))` | `-1` |
| `eq(parse("1.2.3+a"), parse("1.2.3+b"))` | `true` |
| `to_string(bump_minor(parse("1.2.3")))` | `"1.3.0"` |
| `to_string(bump_major(parse("1.2.3")))` | `"2.0.0"` |
| `satisfies_caret(parse("1.3.0"), 1, 2)` | `true` |
| `satisfies_tilde(parse("1.3.0"), 1, 2)` | `false` |
